    <!-- THE PACK SIZE, and it is stated in FOUR strings (#219). Change one and
         you change all four: lang_sheet_space_body and lang_sheet_data_body
         here, offline_subtitle below, and settings_mobile_data_supporting in
         :feature:settings. Two of the four said ~30 MB and were contradicted by
         every measurement this project has.

         40–65 MB is not an estimate and not two samples. It is the on-disk size
         (SZ) of all 58 translate models declared in
         res/raw/translate_models_metadata.json inside translate-17.0.3.aar —
         the version this app builds against — min 39.5 MB (be_en), max 63.4 MB
         (en_ja), median 43.7. Trusted over the old guess because af_en's
         declared SZ is 44,169,505 bytes and the E-S1 device walk measured
         44,169,505 bytes: byte-identical, so SZ is the real footprint.

         The DOWNLOAD is smaller (DL_SZ, 31.3–48.0 MB) and the sentences do not
         claim otherwise — each states how big a pack IS, and the mobile-data
         pair carries the charge warning separately. Overstating a data estimate
         costs a user nothing; understating a size is the harm #219 was filed
         about. Full derivation: docs/plan/issue-219-copy-sweep.md §1. -->
    <!-- Sheet 19b — the download was refused before it started, because the disk
         cannot hold a pack (the 150 MB pre-flight in RealOfflineModelManager —
         which is not this figure and is not meant to be: a download holds the
         compressed file AND the unpacked pack at once, 111.4 MB peak for en_ja.
         What 19b should SAY about that gap is a design call, residual on #250).
         The bar is used-against-free on ONE volume and never packs-against-
         device: at 110 MB the library cannot be plotted against a whole device
         without misstating one of the two figures (spec rev 5). The drawn second
         action, "Free up space", opens 20e, which is PR-25 — omitted rather than
         wired to nothing, per the rev3 ruling. -->
    <string name="lang_sheet_space_title">Not enough space</string>
