    <!-- Offline-library meter, foldable two-leaf (17b / U-5). The big numeral is
         its own key so locales with their own digits shape it; the line beside it
         carries the denominator (offline-CAPABLE, as above) and the size.
         THREE detail lines, not one with a blank: each says something the app has
         actually established. `_used` needs a measured walk of ML Kit's model
         store. `_free` is what it says when that walk cannot answer, because
         "0 MB used" would be a claim about the disk that nothing checked — and
         that is not a rare state: a pm clear on emulator-5554 drew
         "1 of 59 packs · 8.6 GB free" on the very first frame, since ML Kit counts
         the English pivot before anything is downloaded (E-S1b). `_none` outranks
         both whenever the count is zero, because a size under a count of nought
         is a size for something the user does not have. -->
    <!-- 18a/18b — the first-run suggestion block (#130 PR-21). Drawn on the source
         picker when the user has no recents yet, in place of the Recent section.
         "No packs yet" is the owner's intentional first-run copy (§8 of the
         designer brief), NOT the offline-library meter's text: the meter is a
         separate element that reads "1 of 59 packs" on a real device (#203). The
         suggestions are derived from the device's own locales, so the block never
         invents a signal the platform will not give — see firstRunSuggestions(). -->
    <string name="lang_first_run_title">No packs yet</string>
    <string name="lang_first_run_body">Pick a language to download once, then it works with no signal.</string>
    <!-- Ruling ④ (#130 PR-28): this line states only what THIS brand can honour.
         The tranzlate waterfall is MLKit-offline → GOT → GCT
         (RealTranslator.kt:41-42; spec 02-…:20 — the two online tiers send "text
         to the cloud"), so a downloaded pack stays on the device but anything
         else is sent over the internet. The unconditional "nothing is sent
         anywhere" that shipped here was false for this brand and is gone. A
         future OFFLINE-ONLY brand — one whose config carries no online tier —
         states the stronger "nothing you type is uploaded" claim by shadowing
         THIS key from its own app/src/<brand>/res/values/strings.xml: app
         product-flavor resources win over a library module's in the resource
         merge, the same white-label override the tranzlate flavor already uses
         for app_name and the launcher icon. This library default is the SAFE
         fallback — it under-claims privacy, never over-claims it, so a brand that
         forgets to override cannot ship a lie. Pinned by FirstRunPrivacyCopyTest. -->
    <string name="lang_first_run_privacy">Downloaded languages translate on your device. Without a pack, your text is sent over the internet.</string>
